Z||000000||Deer_Slayer||06-15-2000||01:05 PM||||   Yesterday, my stepdad brought the 86 SE back home from the friend of his who repainted it.  I tell you, he did one heck of a job on it!  He sprayed the roof, dechlid, and rear quarter pannels and facia.  He blended the paint on the doors and winshield posts to where no one can tell it was painted in the first place.  The cost for the job was $300.  The only things to do now are replace the rack, "2m4" decal, cracked sailpannels, and repaint the black.    ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Oreif||06-15-2000||02:54 PM||||If you find an 84 SE get the sail panels off of it for your car. (or get one from Twin Lake, Kick Hill, Fiero Factory, ETC) They are GLASS not plastic! That's what I did on my 86 SE. You can also get new Pontiac emblems from a dealer. (The little red ones that go on the sail panel.) The glass ones won't crack and look great.||||reg||3
